Last weeks #Omnivore screening was a success! Thanks to everyone that joined us and a special thanks to Matt Goulding, co-creator of Omnivore, for joining our Q&A and Robert Olinger, for conducting said Q&A. 

We loved hearing everyones questions and insights from Areli and Matt. It was so great to see the adventure of coffee making its way from Rwanda to Durham. Puts it all into perspective. 

@appletv

@coffeereview rated Humure Abishyizehamwe with a 94, thanks so much!! We are so happy to have this special coffee recognized and it was also featured in Apple TV+ "Omnivore." 

Coffee Review's bottom line: "A delicate, enticing, richly sweet Rwanda processed by a natural method that is a kind of soft anaerobic, as some oxygen is allowed during the whole-cherry fermentation process."

sourced @bahocoffee via @sundogtrading 

@appletv #omnivore

Have you seen the Omnivore episode yet? These are some stills from the episode that capture the practices of the roastery. 

There are days in the roastery where you can catch the team performing a cupping, checking in on our coffees, and there are days where the @cocoacinnamon team and wholesale partners are learning more about our coffees, expanding palates. Very grateful for these recorded moments. 

